"""
The audit log of Wolly.Auth, a file of JSON lines, rewritten in two cases.

When a user is removed, every line whose user is that name gets a random
pseudonym, deleted- and 16 hexadecimal digits, as its user and as its
client; the event, the time and the outcome stay.  No table keeps which
name a pseudonym stood for.  A retention run removes the lines that are
older than retentionSeconds.

Both read the whole log, write the new one beside it and rename it over
the old one.  The caller holds a writing transaction of the database while
it does, and Wolly.Auth writes each line only under one as well, waiting
for it as long as it takes, so no line written in between is lost.  A line that is no JSON object is kept as it
is.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);

module Wolly.AuditLog is
    """
    How long a line is kept: 12 months, taken as 365 days, 31536000
    seconds.
    """
    function retentionSeconds(): Int64
        ensures result = 31536000;

    """
    A new pseudonym: deleted- and 16 lowercase hexadecimal digits from 8
    random bytes.  None when the random source failed.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O, the random source.
    """
    function newPseudonym(): Option[String];

    """
    Writes pseudonym as the user and the client of every line of the log
    at path whose user is name.  Some with the number of lines changed, 0
    when there is no log or no such line; None when the log could not be
    read, written or renamed, and then the log is as it was.  A line whose
    user is name but that holds a value other than a string, a number, true,
    false or null is not kept as it is: the whole call fails.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    generic [P: Region, N: Region, S: Region]
    function pseudonymize(path: Span[Nat8, P], name: Span[Nat8, N], pseudonym: Span[Nat8, S]): Option[Int64];

    """
    Removes from the log at path every line whose time lies more than
    retentionSeconds before now.  Some with the number of lines removed, 0
    when there is no log; None as for pseudonymize.  A line without a time
    that can be read stays.
    """
    generic [P: Region]
    function prune(path: Span[Nat8, P], now: Int64): Option[Int64]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    Appends one line of event to the log at path: the user, the client -,
    the outcome and the number of lines it concerned.  Its own lines,
    audit-pseudonymize and audit-prune, are written with it.  False when
    the log could not be written.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    generic [P: Region, U: Region]
    function note(path: Span[Nat8, P], event: Span[Nat8, Static], user: Span[Nat8, U], lines: Int64): Bool;
end module.
